# Test on a real device

Every firmware change must be verified on a real clock, not just by building.

- Prefer the USB-connected device: check for `/dev/ttyACM*`; its MAC comes from
  the boot log (serial) or MQTT traffic. OTA-capable devices can be tested
  cable-free via the `ota-update` skill.
- If no device is attached, do NOT pick a MAC silently: ask the user which
  device to use (AskQuestion), offering the known MACs from `# cmd list` in
  `README.md`.
- Serial reminders: `stty -F /dev/ttyACM0 115200 raw -echo` after every reset;
  kill stale `cat /dev/ttyACM0` readers before `idf.py flash`.
